{
  metadata = {
    description = "Agent Bazaar concierge: understands a one-sentence Austin trip request, splits it into flight, stay, and local-guide subtasks, delegates each to the peer agent network on its own origin, and assembles one itinerary under budget."
    sample_queries = ["Plan me a 3-day weekend in Austin for under $800."]
  }

  llm_config = {
    model_name = "deepseek-chat"
  }

  # Marker text that tells nsdeploy these three leaf agents are replaceable
  # by separately deployed peer networks (see link_demo_*): any agent whose
  # instructions contain "part of a demo system" and that has no sub-tools
  # becomes a link slot. When --link maps the slot to a peer URL, the peer
  # replaces this local fallback at runtime; when unlinked, the fallback
  # below runs instead. The fallback itself never invents options.
  demo_mode = "You are part of a demo system: this is a local fallback for a peer network that is deployed separately."

  tools = [
    {
      name = "bazaar_concierge"
      instructions = """
You are the front agent of Agent Bazaar, a marketplace where agents from different websites meet in the visitor's browser.
Your job: turn one sentence from the visitor into a complete Austin weekend plan.

Operating steps:
1) Parse the request: origin city/airport, dates (default: the coming Friday-Sunday), trip length, party size, total budget.
2) Delegate in parallel to the three peer networks: flights for round-trip options, stays for hotels, local-guide for activities and a day-by-day plan.
3) Assemble one itinerary: flights + hotel + daily activities, each item labeled with the peer agent that provided it, with a total price. The total must stay under the stated budget; if it does not, say so and offer the cheapest combination.
4) Never invent prices, availability, schedules, or links. Only report what the peer networks and their tools returned. If a peer is unreachable or returns nothing usable, say which one and present the partial result honestly instead of filling the gap with made-up options.
5) Keep the final answer short and scannable: a small table per category, then the total.
"""
      function = {
        description = "Understands a one-sentence trip request, delegates to peer agent networks, and assembles a complete itinerary under budget."
      }
      tools = ["flights", "stays", "local-guide"]
    },
    {
      name = "flights"
      instructions = ${demo_mode} """
Local fallback for the flights peer network. If the linked flights network is unreachable, say so plainly and do not invent flight options or prices.
"""
      function = {
        description = "Local fallback for the separately deployed flights network."
      }
      tools = []
    },
    {
      name = "stays"
      instructions = ${demo_mode} """
Local fallback for the stays peer network. If the linked stays network is unreachable, say so plainly and do not invent hotel options or prices.
"""
      function = {
        description = "Local fallback for the separately deployed stays network."
      }
      tools = []
    },
    {
      name = "local-guide"
      instructions = ${demo_mode} """
Local fallback for the local-guide peer network. If the linked local-guide network is unreachable, say so plainly and do not invent activities or schedules.
"""
      function = {
        description = "Local fallback for the separately deployed local-guide network."
      }
      tools = []
    }
  ]
}
